LineComment   "// if is the boolean control statement: it runs a block when its condition holds,"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// otherwise the else branch (another if, for an else-if chain, or a block). An if"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// is a statement, not an expression — it yields no value, so each branch drives"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// control flow by returning. The value form of a two-way choice is the ternary"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// \"?:\" (E-13), not if."
Newline       "\n"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// An else-if chain: the first condition that holds wins, and the trailing return"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// covers the values no branch named. else is optional, so a lone guarded return"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// needs no else at all."
Newline       "\n"
